Claus is a mortal, 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
Yet a time is sure to come when every mortal who has grown old and
lived his life is required to leave this world for another;

Claus has everlasting life (after receiving the Mantle), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
And Claus slept on, the red blood of everlasting life coursing swiftly
through his veins;

Ak is a Master Woodsman of the World, 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
These were Ak, the Master Woodsman of the World, who rules the forests
and the orchards and the groves;

Ak rules forests, orchards and groves (throughout the world), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
These were Ak, the Master Woodsman of the World, who rules the forests
and the orchards and the groves;

Prince of the Knooks is a king (of the Knooks), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
In addition to the immortals I have named were the King of the Knooks,
who had come from his home in the jungles of India;

Claus is loved by Ryls (for his laughter), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
And the Ryls loved the sound of his laughter;
the Knooks loved his courage; the Fairies loved his innocence.

Claus is loved by Knooks (for his courage), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
And the Ryls loved the sound of his laughter;
the Knooks loved his courage; the Fairies loved his innocence.

Claus is loved by Fairies (for his innocence), 1902, The Life and Adventures of Santa Claus
And the Ryls loved the sound of his laughter;
the Knooks loved his courage; the Fairies loved his innocence.
